2. User Materials and Application Output

For purposes of this License, "User Materials" means player names, player
settings, key bindings, window state, custom crosshair data, imported
skins, world edits, save data, Othello settings, user-created text,
user-created images, user-created video, chat content, AI workbench history,
and other materials that a user independently creates, inputs, edits,
records, or prepares through ordinary use of the Ludoxel application.

For purposes of this License, "Application Output" means ordinary
screenshots, screen recordings, save files, logs, generated AI workbench
records, rendered states, configuration files, and other output produced
by the Ludoxel application through ordinary application use.

User Materials do not become Original Materials merely because they are
entered, edited, generated, saved, exported, displayed, recorded, or
shared through the Ludoxel application.

Subject to this License and to applicable third-party rights, a user
may use, record, reproduce, publish, and share that user's own User
Materials and Application Output, including ordinary screenshots, ordinary
screen recordings, save data, and user-created AI workbench output.

The preceding permission does not authorize copying, extracting, modifying,
publishing, distributing, deploying, incorporating, relicensing, selling,
sublicensing, creating derivative works from, representing as one's own,
or using as training data any Original Materials, third-party materials,
repository text, implementation text, visual assets, bundled resources,
project-specific textures, branding material, application icons, user
interface assets, shaders, or any substantially derived work based on them.

If User Materials or Application Output contain a material part of the
Original Materials, third-party materials, repository text, user interface
text, visual assets, bundled resources, project-specific textures, branding
material, application icons, or other protected content, the included
protected material remains subject to its applicable legal terms.

No statement in this Section 2 represents that User Materials or Application
