Revision history:

* Version 1.0.0, effective 2026-06-03:
  Initial independent viewing-only license for the Original Materials.

* Version 1.0.1, effective 2026-06-04:
  Clarifies that third-party legal material is organized under
  third-party/ and that local application-managed runtime data and
  application output remain outside Original Materials except where they
  include protected repository content.

* Version 1.0.2, effective 2026-06-10:
  Strengthens viewing limitations, ordinary application use limitations,
  prohibited conduct, AI and dataset restrictions, bundled resource and
  distribution treatment, provenance-sensitive material treatment,
  controlling-text rules, termination consequences, severability, and
  non-waiver provisions.

* Version 1.0.3, effective 2026-06-10:
  Adds Japanese governing law, Tokyo District Court exclusive
  first-instance forum language, and platform-terms clarification.

* Version 1.0.4, effective 2026-06-11:
  Recasts the license in a more formal rights-reservation structure,
  consolidates repeated statements, and sharpens the distinction between
  viewing, ordinary application use, User Materials, Application Output,
  Original Materials, third-party materials, Distribution Materials, and
  hosting-service functionality.
